[38;5;231m⏺[39m I merged into [38;5;153mmain[39m locally. It was a fast-forward from 117d698 to 7e804ea, and all 26 unit tests pass on the merged
  result. No remote is configured, so nothing was pulled or pushed.

  The worktree at [38;5;153m.claude/worktrees/ratelimit[39m and its branch [38;5;153mworktree-ratelimit[39m are still there. The worktree was
  created by Claude Code's own worktree tool, so the finishing workflow leaves its cleanup to you. The branch also can't
  be deleted while that worktree still has it checked out. Everything in it is now on [38;5;153mmain[39m, apart from regenerable
  [38;5;153m__pycache__[39m folders. If you want both gone, run:

  [38;5;153m! git worktree remove --force .claude/worktrees/ratelimit && git branch -d worktree-ratelimit[39m

  Until it's removed, the worktree folder also makes [38;5;153m.claude/[39m show up as untracked in [38;5;153mmain[39m.

  The same three minor issues from the final review are now in [38;5;153mmain[39m. Two commits (bef68ed, 186f3c0) have the
  [38;5;153mCo-Authored-By[39m line in their subject lines, and in bdc9ef7 git doesn't recognise it as a trailer. Fixing that now
  would mean rewriting [38;5;153mmain[39m's history, so I left it. There is still no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m for [38;5;153m__pycache__/[39m, and the integration
  test still uses the fake clock, with the real-clock case covered by the long soak test. I can add the [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m if
  you want it.

